# VideoBrief — Architecture

## Layout

```text
Browser
  → Next.js (RSC + thin Server Actions + TanStack Query where needed)
      → domain/application logic
          → Drizzle / Supabase
          → enqueue BullMQ `analyze` job (Redis)
Worker
  → loop continueAnalysis (one stage)
      → TranscriptProvider (youtubei.js)
      → AIProvider (Vercel AI SDK; model from analysisConfig)
```

Server Actions authenticate, authorize, validate input, then call domain functions. **Do not** embed the analysis pipeline in actions or React components.

Redis is queue + lock + usage counters only. Do **not** store transcripts or sections in Redis.

## Library preview vs Generate

| Step | DB | Usage | Queue |
|------|----|-------|-------|
| Preview URL (metadata) | none | no | no |
| Generate | upsert `user_videos` + analysis | yes | enqueue analyze |

Preview is a thin authenticated action (or domain call) returning metadata only. Generate creates the library entry, writes prefs + `run_id`, consumes the monthly slot, enqueues, and **redirects to the workspace**.

## Per-user video data

Each library entry is one row per `(user_id, youtube_id)`:

- `user_videos` — metadata + English transcript snapshot (refreshed on every Generate/re-run)
- `personalized_analyses` — state machine, 0–100 prefs (length, tone, optional familiarity), `run_id`, overview `summary`, generated sections (1:1 with `user_videos`)

Re-running the same URL **always resets** analysis (new `run_id`, clear summary/sections) and refetches from YouTube. There is **no shared global cache** across users.

Profile defaults (typed): `summary_tone`, `summary_length` (0–100). Per-video prefs override on the analysis row.

## Analysis states

`pending` → `fetching` → `generating` → `complete` | `failed`

No `classifying` stage. UI communicates progress without leaking Redis/BullMQ/`runId`.

## AIProvider

```text
generateSections  # { summary, sections: { title, startTime, endTime, body }[] }
```

No `classifyVideo`. Domain owns the pipeline. Callers must not import a vendor SDK.

## Suggested folder sketch

```text
src/
  app/                 # routes, layouts, loading/error
  components/          # UI (shadcn + feature)
  domain/              # analysis pipeline, pure-ish business logic
  db/                  # drizzle schema, client
  lib/                 # supabase, ai, youtube, queue, utils, actions
  worker/              # BullMQ analysis runner (not imported by Next)
  hooks/
  messages/            # next-intl (en.json)
```

## Cost awareness

Generate is the expensive call (transcript subset + per-video prefs). Cap generate output tokens. Model id lives in `analysisConfig`, not env. Preview must not call the LLM.
